# A subtree between documents, and the address an entry of them is filed under. Both are written to a
# store and read back by whatever build is running when the document that was owed the rows takes them,
# which is every reason the state types below are pinned here.
# A hand-over gained two fields when it started being written in pieces, and the absent value is the
# right answer for both, which is why the identity is not bumped. An entry written before there were
# pieces holds all of its rows in `changes` and has no further ones - which is what `batches` reading 0
# says - and it was written at the address of the hand-over itself, which is what `piece` reading 0 is.
io.tapstate.runtime.engine.nest.ParkedSubtree :: field :: batches :: int
io.tapstate.runtime.engine.nest.ParkedSubtree :: field :: changes :: java.util.List<io.tapstate.runtime.engine.nest.NestElement>
